Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:

##### Sets and Indices

- $S = \{\text{I}, \text{II}\}$: set of schools, indexed by $s$
- $N = \{\text{N01}, \ldots, \text{N31}\}$: set of neighborhoods, indexed by $n$

##### Parameters

- $C_s$: capacity of school $s$
    - $C_{\text{I}} = 2028$
    - $C_{\text{II}} = 1560$
- $P^{W}_n$: white population in neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- $P^{NW}_n$: nonwhite population in neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- $d_{s,n}$: distance in miles from school $s$ to neighborhood $n$ (see table below)
- District-wide white percentage: $p^W = 0.6$, nonwhite $p^{NW} = 0.4$
- Allowed deviation: $0.1$ (10 percentage points)

##### Decision Variables

- $x^{W}_{s,n} \geq 0$: number of white students assigned from neighborhood $n$ to school $s$
- $x^{NW}_{s,n} \geq 0$: number of nonwhite students assigned from neighborhood $n$ to school $s$

##### Objective

Minimize total travel distance:
$$
\min \sum_{s \in S} \sum_{n \in N} d_{s,n} \left( x^{W}_{s,n} + x^{NW}_{s,n} \right)
$$

##### Constraints

1. **Neighborhood population assignment:**  
   For all $n \in N$,
   $$
   \sum_{s \in S} x^{W}_{s,n} = P^{W}_n
   $$
   $$
   \sum_{s \in S} x^{NW}_{s,n} = P^{NW}_n
   $$

2. **School capacity:**  
   For all $s \in S$,
   $$
   \sum_{n \in N} \left( x^{W}_{s,n} + x^{NW}_{s,n} \right) \leq C_s
   $$

3. **Racial balance at each school:**  
   For all $s \in S$,
   $$
   0.5 \leq \frac{\sum_{n \in N} x^{W}_{s,n}}{\sum_{n \in N} \left( x^{W}_{s,n} + x^{NW}_{s,n} \right)} \leq 0.7
   $$
   (i.e., white percentage at each school must be between 50% and 70%)

4. **Nonnegativity:**  
   $$
   x^{W}_{s,n} \geq 0,\quad x^{NW}_{s,n} \geq 0 \qquad \forall s \in S, n \in N
   $$

